Per-machine extra root CAs for the sandbox image (TLS-intercepting proxies).

Drop PEM certificates here as *.crt before building; they are gitignored and
never committed. Use neutral file names (ca-1.crt, ca-2.crt, ...) if the
originals carry identifying names. Typical source on a host that already
trusts the interceptor:

    i=0; find /usr/local/share/ca-certificates -name '*.crt' | while read f; do
      i=$((i+1)); cp "$f" docker/extra-ca/ca-$i.crt; done

Then rebuild:  python scripts/setup_check.py --container --build-image
A successful build prints "[extra-ca] registered N extra cert(s)".
